// ═══ finally ALWAYS executes — normal flow ═══
try {
    BigDecimal balance = getBalance("SAV2001");
    log.info("Balance: {}", balance);
} catch (AccountNotFoundException e) {
    log.error("Account not found: {}", e.getMessage());
} finally {
    log.info("FINALLY: cleanup runs regardless!");
    // Runs after try (success) OR catch (exception).
    // Use for: close connections, release locks, clean temp files.
}

// ═══ finally executes even with RETURN in try ═══
public BigDecimal getBalanceSafe(String accountId) {
    try {
        return getBalance(accountId);  // returns here...
    } catch (Exception e) {
        return BigDecimal.ZERO;  // or here...
    } finally {
        log.info("FINALLY: runs EVEN AFTER return!");
        // Runs BEFORE the return value is actually sent to caller!
        // (Caution) Don't put "return" in finally — it overrides try/catch returns!
    }
}

// ═══ finally with return — GOTCHA! ═══
public int gotcha() {
    try {
        return 1;
    } finally {
        return 2;  // (Caution) OVERRIDES try's return! Method returns 2, not 1!
        // NEVER return from finally — confusing, error-prone!
    }
}
```

Four situations where finally does NOT execute:

```java
// 1. System.exit() — JVM shutdown:
try {
    System.exit(0);  // JVM terminates HERE
} finally {
    log.info("NEVER PRINTED!");  // ← NEVER executes!
    // System.exit triggers shutdown hooks but NOT finally blocks.
}

// 2. JVM crash (native error, kill -9):
// If the JVM process is killed (SIGKILL, segfault, OOM killing):
// → finally does NOT execute. Nothing can run — process is dead.

// 3. Runtime.halt() — immediate shutdown, no cleanup:
try {
    Runtime.getRuntime().halt(1);  // IMMEDIATE stop — no shutdown hooks, no finally!
} finally {
    log.info("NEVER PRINTED!");
}
// halt() vs exit(): exit runs shutdown hooks. halt runs NOTHING.

// 4. Infinite loop or deadlock in try/catch:
try {
    while (true) { }  // infinite loop — never reaches finally!
} finally {
    log.info("NEVER REACHED!");  // unreachable code!
}
// Thread.sleep(Long.MAX_VALUE) in try → same problem. Deadlock → same.
```

Modern replacement — try-with-resources:

```java
// ═══ OLD: finally for cleanup ═══
Connection conn = null;
try {
    conn = dataSource.getConnection();
    // use connection
} catch (SQLException e) {
    log.error("DB error", e);
} finally {
    if (conn != null) {
        try { conn.close(); } catch (SQLException e) { log.error("Close failed", e); }
    }
    // 5 lines of cleanup! Verbose!
}

// ═══ NEW: try-with-resources (Java 7+) ═══
try (Connection conn = dataSource.getConnection()) {
    // use connection
} catch (SQLException e) {
    log.error("DB error", e);
}
// conn.close() called AUTOMATICALLY when try block exits!
// Even if exception occurs. Even if catch throws.
// 0 lines of cleanup! Clean!
// Works for ANY class implementing AutoCloseable.
```

